From e873dc0a38a736fff004c9a4201f1883eee09d5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:29:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] runtime: stream a frame that has only a quad layer

A frame whose layers are a single quad and no projection layer (a game's
loading screen, or a menu drawn on one quad) streamed nothing: the encoder
only ran when a projection layer was present, so the headset kept its last
picture, or none, for the whole loading screen. Such a frame now streams
the first quad, placed per eye where it sits in space: each display pixel
is ray-cast onto the quad's plane and lands on black outside it.
